                817,
                151
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Center T-slot offset with respect to Axis of Pivot.",
            "block_bbox": [
                514,
                160,
                902,
                203
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "PROCEDURE:",
            "block_bbox": [
                514,
                225,
                653,
                246
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A test bar is inserted in the spindle, a run out test conducted, and the bar turned to place the mean position of eccentricity error in the horizontal plane.",
            "block_bbox": [
                513,
                249,
                904,
                337
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The saddle-table assembly is swiveled so that the center T-slot is parallel with the axis of the spindle.",
            "block_bbox": [
                513,
                338,
                906,
                402
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A DIAL INDICATOR is attached to a jig. The jig is placed in the center T-slot against one side of the T-slot throat. When this is accomplished, the plunger of the instrument is adjusted to touch the test bar at the horizontal diameter, and a reading is taken.",
            "block_bbox": [
                511,
                403,
                901,
                556
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The DIAL INDICATOR and jig are transferred intact to the other side of the throat of the center T-slot. The reading is noted. The difference in readings denotes the amount of offset of the center T-slot with respect to the axis of the pivot.",
            "block_bbox": [
                509,
                557,
                908,
                710
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 15
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The tolerance allowed is indicated in Fig. 27.99. If the tolerance is exceeded, the reason may be found by reference to Sec. 27.81.",
            "block_bbox": [
                508,
                711,
                893,
                800
            ],
